=== PARITY (vs web FSMDistributionWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (FSMDistributionSource -> FSMDistributionModel):
    useVehicles, useFSMStats(GET /fsm/stats?vehicle_id), useFSMTransitions(GET /fsm/transitions?vehicle_id&fsm_name=vehicle
    &hours=24&page=1&per_page=5), useTranslation. The production app wires the source over the KMP FSM store
    (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>); the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection -> FSMDistributionBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web memos:
    • stateColor: case-insensitive map of the 5 STATE_COLORS keys (driving/charging/asleep/idle/offline), else gray.
    • buildDonutData: filter durations >0, total, drop when total==0 (web `if (total===0) return []`), {state,value,pct},
      sort largest-first (stable → equal durations keep server order). Stats values are ms (web `fmtDuration(ms)`).
    • fmtDuration(ms): totalMin=ms/60000, hrs=floor(totalMin/60), mins=round(totalMin%60) → "Xm" / "Xh Ym".
    • transitions: newest-first, from/to coalesced to "—" (web `?? '—'`); the view caps to 3 (compact) / 5 (standard).
    Verified by 31 EXECUTED XCTest methods (see GATE [1]).
  Composition -> widget shell chrome (GitBranch icon in cyan/statusInfo + "State Distribution" title + freshness chip +
    refresh + optional open) · compact (cols<=1, web `isCompact`) shows the dominant state's color dot + label + duration
    · standard shows the Swift Charts donut (innerRadius .55 = web 55%, angular-inset 2 = web paddingAngle 2, per-state
    color, tap-to-focus center read-out = native analog of the web hover DonutTooltip) + a wrapping centered legend
    (state dot + label + fmtInt(pct)%) + the "Recent Transitions" feed (from→to chips + relative time). All web branches.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion / TSSkeleton + DashboardWidget* infra
